# Python / FastAPI backend conventions

This covers the Legistar scraper, the `dashboard/` FastAPI app, and root-level
scraper scripts. Match the patterns already used in `dashboard/routes/*.py`,
`dashboard/*.py`, and `tests/*.py` rather than introducing new ones.

## Module structure

- Start every module with a one-line docstring describing its purpose
  (e.g. `"""Civic data pages and Socrata-backed JSON APIs."""`).
- Follow immediately with `from __future__ import annotations`.
- Use relative imports within the `dashboard` package (`from ..city_budget import ...`,
  `from .deps import RouteDeps`).
- Group imports: stdlib, then third-party (`fastapi`, `requests`, etc.), then local
  relative imports — each group separated by a blank line.
- Guard import-only-for-typing dependencies behind `if TYPE_CHECKING:` (see
  `dashboard/routes/deps.py`) instead of adding runtime import-cycle workarounds.

## Routes

- New route groups live in `dashboard/routes/<name>.py` and expose a single
  `register(app: FastAPI, deps: RouteDeps) -> None` entry point, wired up in
  `dashboard/routes/deps.py::register_all_routes`.
- Route modules should not reach into global state directly — take everything
  they need from the injected `RouteDeps` instance.
- Raise `HTTPException` for upstream/user-facing errors; wrap third-party
  exceptions in a small helper (see `_socrata_http_error`) rather than leaking
  raw exception text.
- Keep business/data logic out of route handlers — delegate to the sibling
  data modules (`city_budget.py`, `council_accountability.py`,
  `campaign_finance.py`, etc.) that expose `get_*_payload()` functions.

## Typing & style

- Add type hints to all function signatures, including return types.
- Prefer `__slots__` on small data-bag classes that get instantiated once per
  process (see `RouteDeps`).
- Use `Path` from `pathlib` for filesystem paths, resolved relative to
  `Path(__file__).resolve().parents[N]` — never hardcode absolute paths.
- Read feature flags/env vars once at module import time (e.g.
  `SCRAPER_ENABLED`), not scattered throughout call sites.

## Testing

- Tests live in `tests/`, named `test_*.py`, using plain `test_*` functions
  (see `pytest.ini`); use `*Tests` classes only when grouping genuinely
  related cases.
- Mark slow/browser-driven tests with `@pytest.mark.e2e` — don't add new
  markers without updating `pytest.ini`.
- Reuse fixtures from `tests/conftest.py` and `tests/dashboard_test_app.py`
  instead of building ad hoc FastAPI `TestClient` setups per test file.
- New scraper/data modules should ship with at least one corresponding
  `tests/test_<module>.py`.

## General

- Keep scraper/backend code dependency-light — check `requirements.txt`
  before adding a new third-party package, and add new deps there.
- Never commit secrets; read config via `python-dotenv` / `os.environ`,
  following the existing `.env` / `.env.example` split.
